# Python Common Native API

The host declares `source.tenant_field` once in its native domain and binds
trusted context once with `Engine.configure(domain, adapter).with_tenant(8)`. Ordinary assignments omit the matching
tenant. Reads, fluent writes, actions and callback engines inherit the binding.

This notebook inspects and executes the complete native program on in-memory
SQLite. Install the native repository's pinned development environment first.
Set `SELECTO_PYTHON_PATH` if the checkout is not a sibling of
`selecto_livebooks`. Verified native source: `e78c7cddb81e470854ceb8ba89c88cca3ef12455`.

## Inspect The Native Program

```elixir
repo = System.get_env("SELECTO_PYTHON_PATH") || Path.expand("../../selecto-python", __DIR__)
IO.puts(File.read!(Path.join(repo, "examples/common_native_api.py")))
```

The sample declares a native domain structure, previews actual SQL and separate
parameters, inserts without `org_id`, then invokes the archive action inside an
inherited transaction. A second callback inserts another row and attempts a
refused foreign-tenant delete. That callback rolls back its preceding insert.
Final scoped rows are `[[2, 8, "Test", "archived"]]`.

## Execute And Verify

```elixir
uv = System.find_executable("uv") || raise "uv executable is required"
{output, status} = System.cmd(uv, ["run", "python", "examples/common_native_api.py"], cd: repo, stderr_to_stdout: true)
IO.puts(output)
if status != 0 or not String.contains?(output, "PASS: Python common native API"), do: raise "Native Python sample failed"
```

The SQLite insert preview binds `[2, "Test", 8, "done"]` to four `?` placeholders. The tenant
stays in SQL even though the calling code omits it. Native permissions,
cardinality, returning, conflict identities and scope rules remain authoritative.
Each action invocation plans and authorizes its own phase; preview never grants
execution authority. Independently scoped root and site columns keep separate
values.

Callbacks are synchronous and sequential on the calling thread/task. They inherit the domain/tenant and expire on completion. Native savepoints isolate nested work; host/external transactions retain ownership. Streaming and awaitable/generator callback returns refuse. Providers without savepoints retain native refusal.

Run `scripts/quality` and `scripts/package-check` in the native checkout for the release gate. Configure its disposable
PostgreSQL integration/observer URLs to enable live service checks. These checks
do not claim live coverage of every other provider or every related read path.
